    "result_text": "The build succeeds with all 34 tests green. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the string `membershipTier` with a numeric `membershipLevel` (1\u20133):\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Replaced the `membershipTier` string/enum property with `membershipLevel` (integer, min 1, max 3), so the generated `OwnerDto` now exposes `membershipLevel` and no longer has `membershipTier`.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a derived, `@Transient` `getMembershipLevel()`: starts at 1, `+1` when an email is present, `+1` when `namesakeCount` is 0, capped at 3 (leaving level 4 reserved for tenure). This computes from fields already assigned at create.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Replaced the old tier-computing expression (which used household member count / GOLD-SILVER-BRONZE logic) with a mapping of `membershipLevel` from the new getter.\n\n4. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 Updated the create audit line to record `membershipLevel={}` (instead of implying a tier) alongside the owner id it already logged, and refreshed the now-stale audit and household-count Javadoc comments that referenced the old GOLD tier.\n\nNote the behavior change is intentional per the spec: household size no longer influences membership (the old GOLD-at-3-members rule is gone), which the `cp23` test confirms (a 3-member household member now scores level 2, not a tier).",
